After 5 months of hacking on version 3.1, I finally managed to ascend
honestly (without copying save files).  The final stats of my
barbarian were

Brogga the Conqueror St:18/** Dx:19 Co:18 In:10 Wi:14 Ch:11 Neutral S:2611323
Astral Plane $:9297 HP:319(340) Pw:141(141) AC:-39 Xp:30/100117612 T:90518 Sati

the final score:  5320746 points.

   I had a hard time in building a strong character: I lost so many
promising candidates either to a fatal doom (e.g. being zapped with a
wand of death) or to foolish actions (e.g. not realizing I was turning
to stone).  Nothing to do about fate, but I finally decided to hack
the X11 interface; now it rings the bell and reverses-video when the
character is in danger (low HP, stoned, sick); I don't consider this
cheating -;)

more on game balance after the ^L (minor spoilers)

Once I got magic resistance (gray dragon scale mail from a lamp
wish), reflection (shield from a potion wish), and a good weapon
(Vorpal from Crom), and using every spoiler in sight, the game was
relatively easy, in hack-and slash style; of course a barbarian is a
good fighter to start with, and is too dumb to use spells.  I just
engraved Elbereth a few times, when I was surrounded by nasties.
After cleaning up the castle, I wished for a ring of conflict and
scrolls of charging (I hadn't find any, so I couldn't write one with
my magic markers).
   Things were then easy for the most part, and I never needed my
amulets of life saving.  I was ready for the endgame (I had a Valkyrie
killed on the air plane in a previous game), and with the help of a
few cursed scrolls of detect gold I rushed to the Astral plane, where
the ring of conflict make things manageable.
   I never had any food problem (found more food rations then I could
carry); I produced *a lot* of holy water, and I used up a most of it
(I choose not to wish for scrolls of genocide, so I had to fight a lot
of Liches, not to speak of the Wizard).  Putting my bag of holding in
a sack avoided a lot of troubles.

PS. I wished for a (blessed +3) shield of reflection rather then for a
blessed figurine of an Archon: in a previous game, I falled through a
trapdoor; when I went back up, the Archon (no longer my pet) easily
got rid of his former master -:(

